      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that but i feel like i'm just being cautious. my inr is 4.2 which is high but not like, bleeding out level high, right? also i'm really busy with work so going back to the clinic is a huge pain. if i just take a standard dose of a vitamin k supplement for a few days, would that logically counteract the warfarin enough to get me back down to like 2.5? just trying to understand how the mechanism works so i can manage it myself.",
